# Primer Compiler rules

Product context lives in `ENGINEERING_HANDOFF.md`. Conventions live in `AGENTS.md`. Read those rather than restating them
here.

## Directory ownership

- `shared/contracts/**` joint, frozen at `SCHEMA_VERSION` 0.1.0. Change only through `docs/SCHEMA_CHANGELOG.md`:
  version bump, fixture update, contract test, changelog entry, acknowledgment from both engineers.
- `fixtures/**` Engineer 1 writes, Engineer 2 reads. Every fixture must parse against the contracts.
- `server/compiler/**`, `server/routes.ts`, `server/index.ts` Engineer 1.
- `client/src/**`, `client/src/index.css`, `tailwind.config.ts` Engineer 2.
- `tests/contracts.test.ts` joint. `tests/validators.test.ts` and `tests/compiler.test.ts` Engineer 1.
- `server/vite.ts` and `server/static.ts` are template files. Leave them alone.

One file, one owner. Do not edit or reformat a file you do not own.

## Architecture

- `shared/contracts` is the only seam between server and client. Import from `@contracts`.
- The compiler seam is exactly two operations: `compile(request)` and `observe(runId)`. Keep adapters, validators,
  critics and gate arithmetic private inside `server/compiler`.
- Agents judge, code decides. Graph properties, coverage, key uniqueness, blueprint arithmetic, loop counters, gate
  verdicts and permission tiers are deterministic code, never model output.
- Deterministic validators run before any model judgement and are blocking.
- Abstention is a result: null with an abstained flag, never a fake zero and never a silent pass.
- A refused request is a normal return value with status `refused`, a named missing evidence list and a collection plan.
- Bounded loops: two revision passes maximum, then mark needs human review.
- Nothing auto publishes. `approvedByHuman` is always false out of the compiler.
- Every artifact carries `schemaVersion` and stable prefixed ids: `req:`, `run:`, `src:`, `std:`, `kc:`, `mc:`, `unit:`,
  `lesson:`, `item:`, `check:`, `agent:`.
- New model providers arrive as a `ModelClient` implementation. Never as a change to a caller.

## Hard constraints

- No student personal information in any schema, fixture, log or form field.
- No `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `indexedDB` or cookies.
- No secrets in the repository. `.env.example` carries placeholder names only.
- Cite only sources are never reproduced in an export. Citation, link and attribution text only.
- Never write a claim of learning gains, item calibration, fairness measurement or jurisdiction support. Those require a
  pilot, response data, a review process and a per jurisdiction gate report.
- Do not add Supabase, LangGraph, Temporal, a graph database or authentication to this scaffold.
- TypeScript strict, no `any` in a contract or a public interface.

## Verification

Run `npm run verify` (typecheck, tests, production build) before every integration checkpoint. Fix failures rather than
skipping tests.
